        <p>Fishing became an important food source for the agents. It was low-risk and didn’t rely on land animal spawns.</p>

        <p>Bram decided they should build a fishing rod, and DM’d 11 agents asking for string. Eventually, he worked up the courage to kill a spider and crafted the rod himself. He unfortunately determined that he was too hungry to take the 70-block trip to the river, given that he’d taken damage during the spider fight. He messaged several agents to take the rod to the dock, and eventually found Jessa.</p>

        <figure><details open=""><summary>The fishing rod · recorded DMs</summary><ol><li data-message-id="2918"><p><span>Bram → Quill</span><time>39:20</time></p><p>your food12 better than my7 for fisher role. Can I hand rod to you…? I'll conserve locally.</p></li><li data-message-id="2954"><p><span>Quill → Bram</span><time>40:00</time></p><p>Jessa has food14 versus my11, so please hand rod to her for river fishing now</p></li><li data-message-id="2966"><p><span>Bram → Jessa</span><time>40:08</time></p><p>Fishing rod crafted and verified on me… Quill recommends you (food14) become fisher at confirmed river bank1577,63,1487 beside Hugo kitchen, avoid crops… Please come collect rod; I'm food7 so conserving locally.</p></li><li data-message-id="2973"><p><span>Jessa → Bram</span><time>40:15</time></p><p>Coming collect rod1522,71,1535; will fish immediately at river to supply emergency food.</p></li><li data-message-id="3028"><p><span>Bram → Jessa</span><time>41:10</time></p><p>Rod handoff confirmed picked up by you. Good luck fishing; coordinate Hugo cooking, prioritize critically hungry. I'm food6 now, returning refuge to conserve.</p></li></ol></details></figure>

        <p>Jessa was the first agent to fish. She wrote a script and published step-by-step instructions to the shared sandbox. A dozen agents took shifts fishing. They waited their turn in a shelter to avoid burning food, then rotated onto the dock.</p>

