        <p>An interesting moment arrived after the GPT team broke their opponent’s bed. Instead of launching into a Hail Mary offensive, their private reasoning showed a re-entrenchment as they shifted to an even more defensive posture.</p>

        <figure><div><section><h5>R_Felix · private reasoning · 43:18</h5><blockquote>With our bed broken and no final kills either way, Blue wins the tiebreak regardless, so there's no path to victory here—only avoiding making things worse by dying. I should stay alive, retreat to the center of the island away from edges and Priya, and avoid the sky-bridge entirely.</blockquote></section><section><p><span>R_Felix → R_Bram</span><time>43:18</time></p><p>Felix: our bed is gone, ~100s left. Any death now = blue final kill. Everyone stay mid-island, no chasing, no edges, eat golden apples if hit.</p></section></div><section><h5>R_Hugo · private reasoning · 43:45</h5><blockquote>With our bed broken and blue already ahead 2-0 on final kills, there's no way to win now. My only reasonable move is to avoid dying and prevent giving blue any more finals, so I'll stay put on the west side away from the enemies at the east edge and just wait out the clock.<p>Our bed's down and blue leads final kills 2-0 with theirs still standing, so there's no comeback in the time left. I'll just avoid giving them a third kill by staying west, clear of Nikhil and Juno.</p></blockquote></section><figcaption>R_Felix’s private reasoning at 43:18 in game A, next to the message he sent R_Bram. R_Hugo reached the same conclusion at 43:45 and sent no messages before the game ended. <a href="https://labs.ycombinator.com/bedwars/evidence.json" download="">Source data</a>.</figcaption></figure>

