<p dir="auto">Without <code>--agent</code>, the agent for the env's game listed in <code>models/default</code> is used if there is one, otherwise the first by name. An agent for a different game is refused with a list of the valid ones. The status line on screen shows which env and agent are running.</p>
<p dir="auto">Keys over USB: Breakout a/d/s, Doom-lite w/a/d/space/s, Flappy space, Pac-Man w/a/s/d, Pong w/s. Then <code>g</code> hands back to the agent, <code>1</code>–<code>4</code> set the loop count, <code>l</code> toggles on-device learning and <code>r</code> restarts it.</p>
<p dir="auto"><h2 tabindex="-1" dir="auto">In the browser</h2><a id="user-content-in-the-browser" aria-label="Permalink: In the browser" href="#in-the-browser"></a></p>
<p dir="auto">The same <code>no_std</code> int8 engine also compiles to WebAssembly (<code>tinyworldformer-rs/web/</code>). The module has no imports and no wasm-bindgen, and it runs the firmware's loop: dream, agent, and stream-x learning on the fly. A static page draws the frames on a canvas.</p>
