            <title><![CDATA[For the first time ever, Google Search is less than 50% of Alphabet's revenue (415 pts)]]></title>
            <link>https://www.kadoa.com/companies/insights/google-search-below-half</link>
            <guid>50291945</guid>
            <pubDate>Thu, 29 Oct 2026 16:42:17 GMT</pubDate>
            <description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://www.kadoa.com/companies/insights/google-search-below-half">https://www.kadoa.com/companies/insights/google-search-below-half</a>, See on <a href="https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=50291945">Hacker News</a></p>
<div id="readability-page-1" class="page"><div class="page" id="content" tabindex="-1"><p>29 Oct 2026</p><div><p>In the quarter to <!-- -->Sep 2026<!-- -->, Google Search made <!-- -->$63.4B<!-- --> of <!-- -->Alphabet's<!-- --> <!-- -->$128B<!-- --> in revenue, or <!-- -->49.7%<!-- -->. It is the first quarter below half since Alphabet began reporting Search revenue separately. In the<!-- --> <!-- -->31<!-- --> quarters before, Search was between <!-- -->52.8%<!-- --> and <!-- -->62.0%<!-- -->.<!-- --> Over the same years, Google Cloud grew from <!-- -->4.4%<!-- --> of revenue to <!-- -->24.1%<!-- -->.</p></div><section><div><p><h2>The quarter to Sep 2026</h2></p></div><dl><p><dt>Search share</dt><dd>49.7%</dd><dd><strong><span>Down </span>5.6 pts</strong> year over year</dd></p><p><dt>Search revenue</dt><dd>$63.4B</dd><dd><strong><span>Up </span>12%</strong> year over year</dd></p><p><dt>Everything else</dt><dd>$64.2B</dd><dd><strong><span>Up </span>40%</strong> year over year</dd></p><p><dt>Google Cloud</dt><dd>$30.7B</dd><dd><strong><span>Up </span>103%</strong> year over year</dd></p></dl></section><section aria-labelledby="search-share"><div><p>Each quarter's revenue from Google Search &amp; other and from Google Cloud, as a share of Alphabet's total revenue. Everything else is YouTube ads, subscriptions and devices, Google Network and Other Bets.</p><p>Dec 2018 to Sep 2026</p></div><div><ul role="tablist"><li role="presentation"></li><li role="presentation"></li></ul><div role="tabpanel" id="_R_jl_-panel-0" aria-labelledby="_R_jl_-tab-0"><p><svg width="842" height="300" viewBox="0 0 842 300" role="img" aria-label="Search and Google Cloud as a share of Alphabet's revenue each quarter, Dec 2018 to Sep 2026" tabindex="0"><line x1="0" x2="668.4" y1="270" y2="270"></line><line x1="0" x2="668.4" y1="237.14285714285717" y2="237.14285714285717"></line><line x1="0" x2="668.4" y1="204.28571428571428" y2="204.28571428571428"></line><line x1="0" x2="668.4" y1="171.428571